 * ones — because disabling a node only stops NEW placement there; a server
 * already running on a disabled/draining node still needs its forwarding
 * kept correct. A node whose agent isn't reachable (or has no token
 * configured yet) fails independently and is reported, never silently
 * skipped and never able to abort another node's sync — the same H5 lesson
 * ("one failure must not cascade") applied one level up.
